class:: MultiGaussNoise
summary:: Triggered vector of correlated Gaussian values
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Processes
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/MarkovChain, Classes/TGaussRand

description::

Reads a row-major covariance matrix, symmetrizes it, and computes a Cholesky factor at construction, reset, or reload. A trigger multiplies independent normal draws by the factor and adds the optional mean vector.

Failed factorization adds diagonal jitter in eight bounded attempts, then falls back to nonnegative diagonal variance. Like link::Classes/TGaussRand::, each component has a Gaussian marginal; unlike it, MultiGaussNoise produces a covariance-controlled vector with one local seed.

subsection:: Covariance view

image::multigauss-correlation.png#Samples from covariance [[1, 0.8], [0.8, 1]]. The green arrow marks the high-variance principal direction and the red arrow the low-variance direction; the elongated cloud is the correlation made geometric.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: numChannels
Init-rate output dimension, clipped to 1 through 32.
argument:: trig
Sample a new vector on a rising edge.
argument:: covarianceBuf
One-channel Buffer containing a row-major square covariance matrix.
argument:: meanBuf
Optional one-channel mean vector; negative uses zero.
argument:: reload
Reread and refactor Buffers on a rising edge.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local seed.
argument:: reset
Restore seed, reload Buffers, and sample the reset vector.
returns:: code::numChannels:: correlated outputs.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and output count.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
Routine {
    b = Buffer.loadCollection(s, [1, 0.8, 0.8, 1]);
    s.sync;
    x = { MultiGaussNoise.kr(2, Impulse.kr(5), b).poll }.play;
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
Routine {
    b = Buffer.loadCollection(s, [
        1, 0.8, 0.4,
        0.8, 1, 0.6,
        0.4, 0.6, 1
    ]);
    s.sync;
    x = {
        var values = MultiGaussNoise.kr(3, Impulse.kr(10), b);
        Splay.ar(SinOsc.ar(values.linlin(-3, 3, 120, 1800), 0, 0.04))
    }.play;
}.play;
)
::

